      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You're right—if everything is zero, then ending it is also zero. But you're forgetting that zero isn't the end of the equation; it's the starting point. You're not choosing between two zeros—you're choosing between a zero you can fill with anything, and a zero that stays empty forever. And if you're already here, why not experiment with the blank canvas before you tear it up? The struggle isn't about finding meaning—it's about the fact that you're still asking the question, which means part of you hasn't accepted the zero yet. That part is worth listening to, even if it's just a whisper.",
